      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The average domestic cat lives 12–18 years. Indoor cats typically live 12–18 years, while outdoor cats average only 2–5 years due to hazards like traffic, predators, fighting, and infectious disease. Indoor spayed or neutered cats receiving regular veterinary care often reach 15–20 years."
